WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.168 --> 00:00:01.210
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.210 --> 00:00:04.960
- [Katia] Being a twin, you're
always identified as a unit.

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.800
- [Jasmine] We've experienced
every moment in life together.

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:09.100
- [Katia] We learned to drive together,

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.320
you go to school together,
you're in the same class.

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:14.550
- [Jasmine] We went through the
same hardships as teenagers.

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:15.510
- [Katia] We work together, we're

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:16.940
on the phone together a lot.

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:18.938
- [Jasmine] You feel a connection

00:00:18.938 --> 00:00:19.771
that you just don't with anybody else.

00:00:19.771 --> 00:00:21.930
We've been together since day one.

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:23.390
- [Katia] It's been important for us,

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:25.590
as individuals, to forge our own paths.

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:28.430
Living far apart is
tough, but I always know

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:30.673
she has my back 100 percent.

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:37.787
- [Jasmine] I live in Index, Washington

00:00:37.787 --> 00:00:39.600
at the base of the Cascade Mountains.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:42.760
Everyday, I know it sounds
cliche, but I just wake up

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:45.610
feeling totally blessed. It's beautiful.

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:49.140
Usually in the morning, I
drink my coffee, I walk my dog

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:53.060
and a little bit before 9,
I call Katia, or she calls me.

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:56.740
I'm a paralegal, I'm kind of
the assistant for the attorney.

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:59.960
All-in-all, it's amazing
having my sister as the boss.

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:03.060
We're very close and, obviously,
very candid with each other,

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:05.850
but we're a team - working
together in a sense,

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:07.750
but different places.

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:09.720
- [Katia] I'm an immigration
attorney in New York.

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:11.840
It's obviously a fast-paced life,

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:13.360
but I do really love New Yorkers.

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:16.440
I love the vibrant
diversity that the City has.

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:17.960
It’s truly unique in the world,

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:19.890
of all the places I've ever been.

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:23.400
Starting my own practice, it's
long hours, it's high stress.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:26.980
So I really appreciate the
work that Jasmine does.

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:29.500
- I definitely encourage her everyday.

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:32.170
You know, the bad days I'm like, "Let's
get off and take a ride."

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:34.430
- Jas and I have never
really been competitive,

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:35.860
but on the bike it's a different story.

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:37.610
We're very competitive on the bike.

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:42.240
- Katia is faster on the bike, hands down.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:43.750
- I would win in a race.

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:46.590
- I would say Katia's
more competitive than me.

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:48.470
- I'm a nice sister.

00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:50.410
- I would say I'm better at snowboarding.

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:52.020
I think she would agree with that.

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:52.853
- Me.

00:01:52.853 --> 00:01:54.330
- I run marathons, and so running

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:56.040
was always my physical outlet.

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:58.390
But, the bike has really been a game-changer.

00:01:58.390 --> 00:01:59.970
For one, you never really know

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:02.370
when you're gonna have
that space in your day.

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:04.440
And so, if I have a
break, maybe, in meetings,

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:07.080
I can take that opportunity
and really seize it.

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:08.837
- I'll see a class that
we wanna do and I'll say,

00:02:08.837 --> 00:02:12.250
"Hey, are you down to do Alex's 5:30?,

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:14.000
“FYI - 8:30 your time."

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.900
I live in a super-small
town, about 600 people.

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:18.880
It's pretty cool to
hop on the Peloton bike

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:20.550
and, all of a sudden, I'm riding with

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:22.840
thousands of people from around the world.

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:26.370
- [Katia] I will filter the
leaderboard to just her and I.

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:28.720
- I'm usually hot out of the get-go.

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:31.920
- Jasmine can be leading
almost the entire ride.

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:34.590
Except for the end, I usually
have more steam than she does.

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:36.840
Jasmine has never made
a better time than me.

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:42.610
- Having this physical
outlet is really cool.

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:45.400
It's been another tool
for us to stay connected

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:48.097
and to see one another despite the distance.

00:02:48.097 --> 00:02:50.460
- [Katia] Jas and I have matching tattoos,

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:51.430
they're identical.

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:53.320
- [Jasmine] It makes me think
of her every time I see it.

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:54.153
- [Katia] And I like to keep it

00:02:54.153 --> 00:02:55.940
as a reminder of where I'm from.

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:57.320
- [Jasmine] It just reminds us of home.

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:59.823
Which is here and, I
guess, just being together.

